-- title:
--   Affine dilatations commute with localisation
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring, $I \subseteq A$ an ideal and $a \in I$ an element of it, let $M \subseteq A$ be a submonoid, and let $A'$ be a commutative $A$-algebra that is a localisation of $A$ at $M$. For an ideal $J$ of a commutative ring $B$ and $b \in J$, write $B[J/b]$ for the dilatation ring [`AffineDilatation.Ring`](def/RingTheory_AffineDilatation.html#L20), namely the $B$-subalgebra $\operatorname{adjoin}_B(\mathrm{gen}\ J\ b)$ of the localisation $B_b =$ `Localization.Away b` generated by the family `gen J b`; by [`AffineDilatation.mem_subalgebra_iff_exists_mem_pow`](thm.html#AffineDilatation.mem_subalgebra_iff_exists_mem_pow) its elements are exactly the $g/b^n$ with $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and $g \in J^n$. The assertion is that there exists an $A$-algebra homomorphism $$\varphi : A[I/a] \longrightarrow A'[I A' / a'],$$ where $I A' = I \cdot A'$ is the image ideal `I.map (algebraMap A A')` and $a'$ is the image of $a$ in $A'$, such that, when $A'[I A'/a']$ is regarded as an $A[I/a]$-algebra via $\varphi$, it is a localisation of $A[I/a]$ at `Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (AffineDilatation.Ring I a) M`, the submonoid of $A[I/a]$ generated by the image of $M$ under the structure map $A \to A[I/a]$. No uniqueness of $\varphi$ is asserted.
--
--   This is the compatibility of affine dilatations (affine blow-ups) with localisation of the base: the dilatation of a localisation $M^{-1}A$ along the localised ideal is the localisation of the dilatation at the image of $M$, so for $M$ the powers of a single element it identifies the dilatation over a standard affine open with a standard open of the dilatation. It is used in the Néron model infrastructure, in the comparison of the dilatation of a closed subscheme with its affine models and in the estimate for the smoothness defect of an affine dilatation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AffineDilatation_exists_algHom_isLocalization_map.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_RingTheory_AffineDilatation

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

theorem AffineDilatation.exists_algHom_isLocalization_map
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (a : A) (ha : a ∈ I)
    (M : Submonoid A) (A' : Type v) [CommRing A'] [Algebra A A'] [IsLocalization M A'] :
    ∃ φ : AffineDilatation.Ring I a →ₐ[A]
        AffineDilatation.Ring (I.map (algebraMap A A')) (algebraMap A A' a),
      @IsLocalization _ _ (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (AffineDilatation.Ring I a) M)
        (AffineDilatation.Ring (I.map (algebraMap A A')) (algebraMap A A' a)) _
        φ.toRingHom.toAlgebra := by sorry
